From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 16:35:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 495/496] [DS4.1] The ported model kernels' Triton originals go

Request inventory 5 found no Triton kernel in any request type; serving runs
the TileLang ports. The DS4.1 package keeps no Triton:

- sparse_mla.py: _requests, _tokens and _chunk (tilelang.metadata's
  requests, tokens and chunk/decode_metadata);
- attention.py: _pages (tilelang.metadata.pages); vLLM's cdiv replaces
  triton.cdiv in the shared geometry;
- compressor.py: _load_partial_state and _save_partial_states
  (tilelang.compress's gather_partial_state and compress);
- nvidia/model_state.py: _gather_lookback_kernel (tilelang.lookback).

Tests that held the TileLang kernels to these Triton kernels hold them to
torch references of the same contracts instead, exactly, rows left alone
included: the metadata kernels (requests, tokens, chunk, pages,
decode_metadata), the state-ring gather (the ring save already had one), and
the lookback window. The references were checked against transliterations of
the deleted Triton code on the tests' inputs (70 metadata and 40 ring cases).
The runner-inputs benchmark's lookback case, which timed the TileLang kernel
against the Triton one, goes. Docstrings state the contracts instead of
naming the deleted kernels.
